  "thesis_interpretation_bullets": [
    "The frozen 784 branch has clean dataset integrity: all rows match across unified features and Gemini 2.5 Pro labels.",
    "Phase2A was excluded from the main quantitative experiments and remains a separate resumable supplement.",
    "Gemini 2.5 Pro labels are highly imbalanced, with joy, anticipation, and trust dominating the label space.",
    "Common labels are much more stable than rare labels; anger is not estimable and fear/disgust are exploratory.",
    "XGBoost has the best macro-F1, while Logistic Regression is almost tied and has the best macro PR-AUC.",
    "Classical tabular models outperform the neural text models in this small, imbalanced frozen setup.",
    "Transformer-derived features, especially Hartmann and GoEmotions, provide the strongest signal for discrete emotion prediction.",
    "NRC binary agreement with Gemini labels is weak, but NRC affect counts contribute to VAD prediction.",
    "Lexicon VAD and Gemini VAD show modest positive correlations but should not be treated as interchangeable scales.",
    "Gemini labels should be framed as a stronger model-based reference label branch, not human ground truth."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Gemini 2.5 Pro labels are model-generated reference labels, not human consensus labels.",
    "The emotion labels are severely imbalanced.",
    "Rare-label metrics are unstable because positive support is very small.",
    "NRC_count > 0 is a broad lexical rule and not a calibrated classifier.",
    "VAD agreement MAE between lexicon and Gemini sources is affected by scale differences.",
    "The main benchmark is limited to the frozen 784 transcript corpus.",
    "Phase2A is not included in the main quantitative benchmark."
  ],
  "phase2a_pause_wording": "The planned 2,000-perfume YouTube transcript expansion was paused because YouTube API quota limits, transcript retrieval IP blocking, low safe-collection yield, and thesis timeline constraints made the full expansion infeasible. The Phase2A artifacts were preserved as a resumable supplement, while all main scoring and evaluation results use the frozen 784-perfume transcript dataset with Gemini 2.5 Pro reference labels.",
  "recommended_next_thesis_step": "Write the Results section around dataset integrity and label distribution, model benchmark comparison, and Stage8 feature-family importance; then use Discussion to explain label imbalance, rare-label limitations, and the Phase2A pause."
}
